    "whyDuo": {
      "fill": "blue",
      "page": "duo",
      "text": "iPhone Duo\n\n• Cover, and open in landscape: status bar, Back/Close, toolbar and tab bar sit on the trailing edge (DuoSideBar)\n• Open in landscape: list and detail side by side, split at the fold; sheets become inspectors beside the content\n• Open in portrait: laid out like an iPad mini. Standard horizontal bars (DuoTopBar, tab bar at the bottom), one full-height view that pushes to detail, filters as a form sheet; only Settings keeps its list beside the detail\n• Book pose: nothing crosses the fold; the reader shows one page per pane\n• Reader: immersive mode hides every control and the status bar; a tap brings them back",
      "w": 380,
      "x": 1092,
      "y": 0
    },
    "whyIphone": {
      "page": "iphone",
      "text": "What changes on every iPhone\n\n• Floating glass tab bar; Search gets its own button (Tab role .search)\n• Large titles and grouped sections in system type and spacing\n• Glass toolbar groups on Work Detail and the Reader\n• Read Aloud lives in a bottom accessory, like Music's mini player\n• The four symbols (Rating, Category, Warnings, Status) on every work, same order everywhere\n• Density kept: words, chapters, kudos and hits stay visible",
      "w": 380,
      "x": 4700,
      "y": 0
    },
